<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Mr Bands' posting loop: every 15 minutes one tick of src/talk/tick.ts reads the paper desk (data-live) and
  picks at most one post (a band closed or opened, a strap change, a fee milestone, the daily numbers, a lesson
  from a closed seat, the Monday stack), vets it through the lint, and hands it to src/talk/x.ts. It does not
  reply to anyone and does not read mentions. It never trades.

  POSTING IS OFF in this file. There is no X_LIVE here, so every tick only appends a draft to
  data-talk/x-drafts.jsonl (and a dry record to data-talk/x-posts.jsonl). Nothing reaches X.

  Install:  mkdir -p data-talk
            cp ops/com.bands.mrbands.talk.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
            launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.bands.mrbands.talk.plist
  Stop:     launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.bands.mrbands.talk
  Halt now: touch data-talk/TALK_STOP   (the next tick, and any tick about to post, stops; rm it to resume)
  Watch:    tail -f data-talk/talk.log   ·   drafts: data-talk/x-drafts.jsonl
  One tick by hand:  DATA_DIR=data-live TALK_STATE_PATH=data-talk npx tsx src/scripts/talk.ts tick

  Going live, in order:
    1. Put X_API_KEY, X_API_SECRET, X_ACCESS_TOKEN, X_ACCESS_SECRET, X_HANDLE and OPERATOR_HANDLE in .env
       (the scripts load .env from the repo; keys never go in this file).
    2. npx tsx src/scripts/talk.ts check   (a read: prints the handle the keys sign in as and whether it is X_HANDLE)
    3. Read a day of data-talk/x-drafts.jsonl.
    4. Add X_LIVE=true to .env, or uncomment the X_LIVE pair below and bootout + bootstrap this job.
       Only the literal "true" turns posting on. To turn it off again, remove it (or touch data-talk/TALK_STOP).

  Cadence (src/talk/tick.ts planTick defaults; an env key here or in .env overrides one, 0 turns it off). The values
  come from Merd's record (Zach's earlier agent, 296 live posts): structure and rhythm, never his words.
    POSTS_PER_DAY             6    loop posts and dry drafts per UTC day (Merd's realized median was 5)
    TALK_MIN_GAP_MIN          90   minutes between two loop posts
    TALK_GAP_JITTER_MIN       45   an event post (close, open, strap, milestone) waits the gap plus 0..45 minutes, the
                                   number fixed by its key (a strap's by the time its change was first seen), so the
                                   15-minute tick over a flat floor does not print the same gap every time (78% of
                                   Merd's same-day gaps sat within 230-250 min); the daily, the lesson and the stack
                                   keep the plain gap
    TALK_WINDOW_POSTS / HOURS 2/6  at most 2 posts in any rolling 6 hours; the daily numbers pass it, everything
                                   else waits
    TALK_NIGHT_POSTS          2    before TALK_DAY_START_UTC (12) at most 2 posts that day; no quiet hours
    TALK_EVENT_POSTS_PER_DAY  4    close, open, strap and milestone share 4 of the 6 slots; the daily and the lesson
                                   keep 2; a losing close is exempt (a loss is never the thing that stays quiet)
    TALK_OPEN_POSTS_PER_DAY   2    opens' share of the event slots (an open not posted is counted by the daily)
    constants, not env:            at most 2 event posts about one pool a day, at most 2 strap posts a day
    TALK_DAILY_HOUR_UTC       14   the daily numbers, which outrank the event kinds from this hour until they go and
                                   pass the window; only the min gap holds them (a post at 13:50 holds them to 15:20)
    TALK_LESSON_HOUR_UTC      18   the lesson from a closed seat
    TALK_STACK_HOUR_UTC       15   the Monday stack
    TALK_LOOP_MILESTONE_SOL   10   the fee milestone step (tick-state milestoneN is 3: the next post is the 40 sol step)
    TALK_RETRY_BACKOFF_MIN    60   after 3 transient X refusals in a row (402, 429, 5xx, unreachable) the tick does not
                                   call X for 60 min, doubling to 360, one line in talk.log per hold (Merd retried one
                                   402 every 15 min for 14 hours and lost 81 posts). On the calendar, not in code:
                                   check the X pay-per-use balance weekly, keep the Mac on mains with automatic
                                   installs off.
  A day under these values: the daily from 14:00 UTC on the first tick the gap allows (up to 90 min later when a
  post went just before), a lesson from 18 UTC when a seat closed, 2-4 event posts
  spread by the window and the jitter, nights capped at 2, 3-5 posts on a typical day and 6 only on a busy one.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.bands.mrbands.talk</string>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/zach/Bands.Finance/mr-bands</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/local/bin/npx</string>
    <string>tsx</string>
    <string>src/scripts/talk.ts</string>
    <string>tick</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>900</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/zach/Bands.Finance/mr-bands/data-talk/talk.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/zach/Bands.Finance/mr-bands/data-talk/talk.log</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>DATA_DIR</key><string>data-live</string>
    <key>TALK_STATE_PATH</key><string>data-talk</string>
    <!-- the paper desk's cycle: data older than 3 cycles (15 min) is stale and nothing about positions goes out -->
    <key>CYCLE_INTERVAL_SEC</key><string>300</string>
    <key>TALK_VENUES</key><string>meteora dlmm</string>
    <!-- going live (step 4 above): uncomment this pair.
    <key>X_LIVE</key><string>true</string>
    -->
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
